        <name>canAllocateContext</name>
        <qualifiedname>themis::llm::ILLMResourcePolicy::canAllocateContext</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>int64_t</type>
          <declname>token_count</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Return true iff an inference request for <computeroutput>token_count</computeroutput> tokens is permitted under the current policy. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Does not modify any state. A value of 0 for the policy&apos;s <ref refid="classthemis_1_1llm_1_1_i_l_l_m_resource_policy_1a3be8ffb71200fa892f109b08f23ce7e1" kindref="member">maxContextTokens()</ref> means unlimited — this method must return <computeroutput>true</computeroutput> for any positive <computeroutput>token_count</computeroutput> in that case.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>token_count</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Total token budget (prompt + completion) requested. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>true when the request fits within the policy. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="include/themis/llm/illm_resource_policy.h" line="68" column="19"/>
